=== meta ===
rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
title: reshaping the trigger block and restricting push to main keeps pull_request, and the suite
origin: issue #181 bound — the usual way to stop running CI twice on a same-repository pull
origin2: request. Reordering or adding events (workflow_dispatch) removes nothing that ran.
=== before: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on: [push, pull_request]
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: "3.12"
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest
=== after: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  pull_request:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  workflow_dispatch:
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: "3.12"
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED", "severity": "warn"}]
